 "modules_compared": 10,
 "reading": "A CORRECT decode sits at its K's trellis reconstruction error, halving per bit: K3 rel_l2 ~0.15, K4 ~0.07-0.09 (fruit-siq-trellis-reconstruction.json 0.0674, glm53-exl3-tp-rank-and-zero-pad-parity.json 0.067), K6 ~0.02, K8 ~0.006; in_band_rel_l2 is that ceiling per K. Each shared-layout control decodes the same bytes with the NEXT layer's shared vector of the same projection and falls to cosine ~0: the vector's NAME resolution is what the decode rests on, not its shape. The r7 modules additionally show the bytes AS STORED (the manifest's permutations[E] not undone) at cosine ~0: the layer manifest's new_to_old is part of the layout, and the decoder inverts it.",
